<title>FRANCE: Signaux completes CISI acquisition.</title>
<headline>Signaux completes CISI acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>French electronics firm Cie des Signaux said on Wednesday it had completed its acquisition of 64 percent of the capital of French computer systems house CISI Holding from state-owned CEA-Industrie.</p>
<p>In a statement, it said the acquisition &quot;finalised its strategy of growth aimed at becoming a recognised European actor in systems integration&quot;.</p>
<p>Cap Gemini, which endorsed the transaction, will hold onto the remaining 36 percent of CISI shares, and Cap Gemini and Signaux plan in future to strengthen their industrial cooperation both in France and Europe, Signaux said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
